# Line endings are LF, everywhere, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this the answer depends on each developer's `core.autocrlf`, which on
# Windows defaults to `true` and asks for CRLF in the working tree. Prettier
# then writes LF back (its `endOfLine` default), and git spends the rest of the
# day announcing that "LF will be replaced by CRLF" for files whose contents
# have not changed. `eol=lf` states the repository's answer once, so the setting
# on any one machine stops mattering.
#
# `text=auto` still lets git decide what is text; only the ending is forced.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must never touch. The geo build writes JSON, which is text, so it
# is deliberately absent from this list.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
